# Force LF for anything that runs as a script or gets parsed by a shell/
# interpreter -- Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true silently flip
# these to CRLF, which breaks bash parsing on Linux/macOS even when the
# script is invoked as `bash script.sh` (bypasses the shebang issue but
# not mid-script \r corruption). Confirmed broke `dev-local.sh` 17 Aug 2026.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.dart text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF -- harmless either way in practice, but
# explicit is better than relying on core.autocrlf being set the same on
# every machine this repo is cloned onto.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Flutter platform-scaffold text files (Android/Windows/Linux/iOS/macOS
# generated + hand-edited native code) were falling through to bare
# core.autocrlf behavior with no rule of their own -- the same trap the
# rules above already close for scripts, just not extended to these
# extensions yet. Confirmed 24 Aug 2026 (FI26082202): committed copies
# are LF, a Windows checkout's Flutter SDK regenerating these can flip
# them to CRLF locally with no code change, masking real future diffs
# as ~140-file noise.
*.h text eol=lf
*.cc text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
*.gitignore text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.bin binary
